; A PROPOSAL, not part of any draft: one parameter on the policy-decision
; Event Object of draft-petrie-vcon-tool-invocation-00, added through
; its $$event-policy-decision-ext socket. It references a signed record
; of that decision, here a decision receipt in a DSSE envelope, by the
; digest of its bytes and, where it is held outside the vCon, by url.
;
; Used together with the core vCon CDDL (draft-ietf-vcon-vcon-core-05)
; and Appendix D of tool-invocation-00; it uses the core rules
; url_value_type, content_hash_type and media_type_value_type, and no
; other socket. Table 3 of tool-invocation-00 keeps content and
; attachment off the policy-decision, and this parameter uses neither.
;
; Not enforced by this CDDL:
; - content_hash covers the exact bytes of the referenced record, and
;   carries a sha512 token as vCon core requires for external content.
; - The record names the same operation_id and attempt as the event
;   that carries this parameter.
$$event-policy-decision-ext //= (
    decision_receipt: decision_receipt_type
  )

decision_receipt_type = {
    ? url: url_value_type,
    content_hash: content_hash_type,
    ? mediatype: media_type_value_type
  }
